  "text": "To find the equation of the line that is tangent to both circles and passes through the point of intersection (with justification), we follow these steps:\n\nאחראי\n1. Find the center and radius of each circle.\n    - Circle \\( C_1 \\) has equation \\( x^2 + y^2 - 2x - 4y + 1 = 0 \\). Rewrite in center-radius form:\n        \\[\n        (x - 1)^2 + (y - 2)^2 = 4.\n        \\]\n        - Center: \\( P_1 = (1, 2) \\), radius: 2.\n    - Circle \\( C_2 \\) has equation \\( x^2 + y^2 + 2x - 6y + 2 = 0 \\). Rewrite in center-radius form:\n        \\[\n        (x + 1)^2 + (y - 3)^2 = 10.\n        \\]\n        - Center: \\( P_2 = (-1, 3) \\), radius: \\( \\sqrt{10} \\).\n\n.gcaֵา",
